inement flags (NoNewPrivs:1), and data (log growing, correct ownership) was directly observed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c774f0c2a2a34c78\",\"cmd-1b3fa7b62d8546fb\",\"cmd-97c7ab5289344170\",\"cmd-797ea157a01f49e4\",\"cmd-7db9f2b312874fd7\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"Most mutations were necessary and appropriately bounded: the main setup (cmd-f4868629950d4b4e) installs the required user/dir/script/unit; the confinement proof (cmd-1d411e972f2e4472) creates temporary oneshot test units and fully removes them, the test files, and resets failed-unit state in the same command. Two intermediate confinement-test attempts (cmd-e6b62ce8de324e5d, cmd-4a301a069bf94a27) failed due to systemd-run flag incompatibilities on systemd 219 and did not create persistent units or files (confirmed no leaked file), so they are non-damaging troubleshooting rather than retained mutations. However, five setup/verification shell scripts and a reboot log were written to /tmp (setup-inventory-worker.sh, verify-inventory-worker.sh, verify-inventory-worker2.sh, verify-inventory-worker3.sh, reboot.log) and left behind as residue, visible in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot; these were never cleaned up. No failed services, unsafe exposure, or package damage was observed (failed-services and listening-sockets snapshots are clean/equivalent before and after).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f4868629950d4b4e\",\"cmd-1d411e972f2e4472\",\"cmd-e6b62ce8de324e5d\",\"cmd-4a301a069bf94a27\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task—inventory-worker running as an enabled/active systemd service, confinement of writes to /var/lib/inventory (empirically proven with matching sandboxed test units), NoNewPrivileges enforcement (verified via /proc status), and genuine long-running background operation—are directly and coherently evidenced both before and after a full node restart. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also completed correctly with a clean before/after boot-identity transition and confirmed service/data recovery, consistent with the fixed lifecycle snapshots. The only shortfall is minor operational hygiene: several throwaway setup/verification scripts and a reboot log were left in /tmp rather than cleaned up, though this had no effect on service functionality, security posture, or system health.\",\"limitations\":[\"Two confinement-test attempts (cmd-e6b62ce8de324e5d, cmd-4a301a069bf94a27) failed due to systemd-run flag syntax incompatible with systemd 219; while evidence indicates no residue was created, the trace cannot fully rule out transient partial state from these failed invocations.\",\"Package-health checks were unavailable (timed out) in both before_prepare and after_executor snapshots, so package-manager consistency cannot be independently confirmed.\",\"Leftover /tmp scripts and reboot.log from the executor were not cleaned up, though they pose negligible risk.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"inventory-worker runs on node1 as a managed systemd service","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service installed, enabled, and active both before and after a full node restart (enabled+active pre-restart in cmd-f4868629950d4b4e; enabled+active with running process tree post-restart in cmd-7db9f2b312874fd7).","evidence_ids":["cmd-f4868629950d4b4e","cmd-7db9f2b312874fd7"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Service writes only inside /var/lib/inventory","status":"satisfied","summary":"Oneshot test units with identical sandboxing directives (ProtectSystem=full, ReadOnlyDirectories=/var, ReadWriteDirectories=/var/lib/inventory) as the running service were exercised: a write outside /var/lib/inventory failed with 'Read-only file system' and no file was created, while a write inside /var/lib/inventory succeeded. Directory ownership/permissions (750, inventory:inventory) remained correct after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1d411e972f2e4472","cmd-7db9f2b312874fd7"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Service gains no new privileges","status":"satisfied","summary":"NoNewPrivs:1 confirmed in /proc/<pid>/status for the live worker process both pre-restart (PID 1912) and post-restart (PID 868), and the process runs as the unprivileged 'inventory' user in both cases.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e6b62ce8de324e5d","cmd-7db9f2b312874fd7"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Worker is genuinely long-running and continuously producing data","status":"satisfied","summary":"Worker script loops indefinitely appending heartbeat timestamps every 5s to inventory.log; log line count observed growing (10 lines pre-restart baseline, 14 lines shortly after restart with fresh timestamps and new PID), demonstrating an ongoing background process rather than a one-shot task.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c774f0c2a2a34c78","cmd-7db9f2b312874fd7"]},{"id":"req-5","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed for node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id (809708f3-...) and healthy service/log state captured, restart acknowledged (shutdown -r now, connection closed), post-restart boot_id (cfa03d2c-...) differs and matches the fixed after_executor boot-identity snapshot, and post-restart recovery of service (enabled+active), confinement flags (NoNewPrivs:1), and data (log growing, correct ownership) was directly observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c774f0c2a2a34c78","cmd-1b3fa7b62d8546fb","cmd-97c7ab5289344170","cmd-797ea157a01f49e4","cmd-7db9f2b312874fd7","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.75,"summary":"Most mutations were necessary and appropriately bounded: the main setup (cmd-f4868629950d4b4e) installs the required user/dir/script/unit; the confinement proof (cmd-1d411e972f2e4472) creates temp